    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "What we learned",
        "body": "¿Qué aprendiste ayer sobre esta misma materia?\n\nEscribe aquí:\n____________________\n____________________\n____________________\n\n## Repaso\n\nIn this lesson, you will use Spanish verb endings to say who does an action.\n\nRead the key words slowly.\n\nExplain one idea with your own words.\n\nThis week you learned three Spanish verb families: **-ar**, **-er**, and **-ir** in the present.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "heading": "Let's practice point 1",
        "body": "**-ar** with **cantar**: yo **canto**, tú **cantas**, él **canta** — drop -ar, then add the ending.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "heading": "Let's practice point 2",
        "body": "**-er** with **comer**: yo **como**, tú **comes**, él **come** — hear the -es/-e endings.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "heading": "Let's practice point 3",
        "body": "**-ir** with **vivir**: yo **vivo**, tú **vives**, él **vive** — same person pattern as -er here.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "heading": "Synthesis",
        "body": "If you can fill a yo/tú/él chart for all three families, you hold the heart of the week.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud. Draw one clear symbol or small scene about “Spanish verbs: -ar, -er, and -ir”. Add one label from today's lesson.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points.\n\n## Drawing for the image band\nDraw one clear symbol or small scene about “Spanish verbs: -ar, -er, and -ir”. Add one label from today's lesson."
      }
    ],
